{% extends "admin/page.njk" %}

{#
  Ports gfadmin/templates/admin/foodbanks_dupe_postcodes.html (23 lines):
  Django renders one bare <ul>, one <li> per duplicated postcode, each
  linking to {% url 'admin:search_results' %}?q=<postcode>. Five deliberate
  divergences, each with its reason:

  a) The postcode still links to /admin/search/?q=<postcode>, as Django's
     does. (An earlier draft of this file dropped that link on the grounds
     that /admin/search/ was unported -- true when it was written, false
     since the search page landed in this same pass.) The owning records and
     their edit forms are linked as WELL, which is the actual improvement.
  b) Grouped, with the owning food bank / location named inline. Django's
     list tells you a postcode is duplicated but not WHICH rows hold it, so
     the only way to find out there is to follow the (here, missing) search
     link. Naming them is what makes the page actionable.
  c) A count, and an empty state. Django renders an empty <ul> and no
     message when there are no duplicates.
  d) Deterministic order (SQL ORDER BY, not Django's unordered set()).
  e) NULL/empty postcodes excluded in SQL -- see dupePostcodes.ts. Django
     lets a NULL location postcode through as a literal "None" row.

  Django's own {% block title %} says "Foodbanks", not what the page is;
  named properly here.
#}

{% block title %}Dupe Postcodes{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="columns">
  <div class="column is-three-quarters">

    <h1 class="title">Duplicate Postcodes <span class="tag is-info is-normal is-light">{{ groups.length }}</span></h1>

    <p class="content is-size-7">
      Postcodes shared by more than one food bank or location. Closed food banks and closed
      locations are included, matching Django. Donation points are not checked &mdash;
      <code>gfadmin/views.py:340-358</code> never looks at them. Matching is exact, so
      &ldquo;SW1A 1AA&rdquo; and &ldquo;SW1A1AA&rdquo; count as different postcodes.
    </p>

    {% if truncated %}
    <div class="notification is-warning is-light">
      Showing the first {{ limit }} duplicated postcodes only. There are more.
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if not groups.length %}
    <p>No duplicate postcodes.</p>
    {% endif %}

    {% for g in groups %}
    <h3 class="title is-6" style="margin-bottom:4px">
      <a href="/admin/search/?q={{ g.postcode | urlencode }}">{{ g.postcode }}</a>
      <span class="tag is-warning is-light">{{ g.places.length }}</span>
    </h3>
    <table class="table is-fullwidth is-hoverable is-narrow" style="margin-bottom:24px">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Kind</th>
          <th>Name</th>
          <th>Food Bank</th>
          <th></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for p in g.places %}
        <tr>
          <td style="white-space:nowrap">
            {% if p.kind == "foodbank" %}
            <span class="tag is-danger is-light">Food bank</span>
            {% else %}
            <span class="tag is-warning is-light">Location</span>
            {% endif %}
            {% if p.is_closed %}<span class="tag is-dark is-light">Closed</span>{% endif %}
          </td>
          <td>{{ p.name }}</td>
          <td><a href="/admin/foodbank/{{ p.foodbank_slug }}/">{{ p.foodbank_name }}</a></td>
          <td style="white-space:nowrap">
            {% if p.kind == "foodbank" %}
            <a class="button is-small is-link is-light" href="/admin/foodbank/{{ p.foodbank_slug }}/edit/address/">Edit address</a>
            {% else %}
            <a class="button is-small is-link is-light" href="/admin/foodbank/{{ p.foodbank_slug }}/location/{{ p.loc_slug }}/edit/">Edit location</a>
            {% endif %}
          </td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {% endfor %}

  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
